.TH OMACHATD 8 "2026-10-01" "OmaChat"
.SH NAME
omachatd \- hosted messaging and local IPC daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omachatd
[--config PATH] [--state PATH] [--socket PATH] [--file-key]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Connects to one hosted server using a pinned Ed25519 server key and a sealed device credential.
The server operator can read messages. This is not end-to-end encryption.
SIGINT and SIGTERM drain requests and shut down without erasing credentials.
SIGHUP validates configuration; changing server or storage settings requires restart.
.SH CONFIGURATION
JSON fields: storage_provider (auto, secret-service, file) and hosted.
The hosted object requires url and pinned_server_public_key; display_name and invite_code are optional.
Use wss:// except numeric-loopback ws:// for tests. Obtain the server key from its operator.
Retired transport settings are rejected. Desktop setup saves a private backup before replacing them.
.SH FILES
Default configuration: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/omachat/config.json.
Default state: $XDG_STATE_HOME/omachat.
Default socket: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/omachat/omachat.sock.
